145","score":[2,1]}],"analyst_view":{"overall":"The Derby of the North at a sold-out Euroborg: Groningen (9th, 15 pts) have one point from their last four league games and went out of the cup to Emmen, while Heerenveen (6th, 21 pts) have won four in a row, including 5-3 against Feyenoord. Coach Dick Lukkien is still recovering from a hip operation, so assistant Casper Goedkoop leads the team with no direct line to Lukkien during the game (OOG TV, FCGfans). Keeper Etienne Vaessen and Hans Hateboer are banned (counted); Goedkoop confirms third-choice Lovro Stubljar will play in goal, and David van der Werff is back in the squad. Heerenveen miss only Hristiyan Petrov (counted). The bans, the derby boost and referee Alex Bos' slightly above-average card rate are already in the numbers.","goals":{"lean":"higher","adjust_pct":3,"call":"Around 3.5 goals","text":"The numbers say 3.4 goals, already counting both sides' scoring runs (17 goals each in their last six), Vaessen's ban (+6% for Heerenveen) and Hateboer's absence. What they can't see is that Groningen go in with third-choice keeper Stubljar (Janse is also out, confirmed by Goedkoop) and without their head coach on the bench, against a confident Heerenveen attack that Goedkoop says is strong on the flanks; a mild +3% to about 3.5."},"corners":{"lean":"same","adjust_pct":0,"call":"Around 10.0 corners","text":"The numbers say 10.0 corners, with Groningen's recent drop in corners (22 in six) already counted. Goedkoop wants to disrupt Heerenveen's wing play, and Heerenveen will look to play through the press and counter, which fits the numbers' fairly even split, so I stay at 10.0."},"cards":{"lean":"same","adjust_pct":0,"call":"Around 4.0 cards","text":"The numbers say 4.0 cards, already including a large derby boost (+39%) and Alex Bos' 3.3 cards a game. The rivalry is real and the stadium is sold out, but that is exactly what the derby boost covers, and both sides have been light on cards lately (counted), so I stay at 4.0."},"shots":{"lean":"same","adjust_pct":0,"call":"Around 28.8 shots","text":"The numbers say 28.8 shots, with Heerenveen's sharp recent shooting (+8%) counted. Groningen's press leaves space for a quick side like Heerenveen, but that open style is what the numbers have measured all season, and Van der Werff's return only restores Groningen's usual side, so I stay at 28.8."},"shots_on_target":{"lean":"same","adjust_pct":0,"call":"Around 10.0 shots on target","text":"The numbers say 10.0 shots on target, with Heerenveen's recent accuracy (+7%) and Groningen's dip (-7%) already in. A third-choice keeper affects how many shots go in rather than how many are on target, and Petrov's absence is a small loss for Heerenveen (counted), so I stay at 10.0."},"sources":["https://www.oogtv.nl/2026/11/fc-groningen-zonder-lukkien-tegen-sc-heerenveen-in-uitverkochte-euroborg/","https://www.feanonline.nl/goedkoop-over-sc-heerenveen-aan-ons-de-taak-om-dat-te-ontregelen/","https://www.fcgfans.nl/goedkoop-over-ontbreken-lukkien-we-missen-hem-met-zijn-kennis/"],"written_at":"2026-11-21T16:22:09Z"},"league":"eredivisie","take":{"applied":true,"written_at":"2026-11-21T16:22:09Z","goals":{"home":1.733,"away":1.717,"total":3.45,"adjust_pct":3.0,"sized":true,"lean":"higher","home_win":0.377,"draw":0.253,"away_win":0.37,"over":{"1.5":0.873,"2.5":0.67,"3.5":0.453},"over_show":{"1.5":0.873,"2.5":0.67,"3.5":0.453,"4.5":0.265,"5.5":0.136},"btts":0.69,"likely_scores":[{"score":"1-1","p":0.109},{"score":"2-1","p":0.082},{"score":"1-2","p":0.081},{"score":"2-2","p":0.07},{"score":"2-0","p":0.048}],"clean_sheet_home":0.18,"clean_sheet_away":0.177,"range":[1,6],"take_line":{"over":{"line":"1.5","p":0.873,"shown":true},"under":{"line":"5.5","p":0.864,"shown":true}}},"corners":{"home":5.371,"away":4.643,"total":10.014,"adjust_pct":0.0,"sized":true,"lean":"same","over":{"8.5":0.649,"9.5":0.533,"10.5":0.418,"11.5":0.314},"over_show":{"8.5":0.649,"9.5":0.533,"10.5":0.418,"11.5":0.314,"12.5":0.226},"ra